  "scope": "One statement-led normalization derivation frozen before target release, followed by a complete five-item comparison, resolves both genuine statement-scope failures. The reduced support S is explicitly singular, as required by the conductor and Kodaira-dimension input; the actual smooth reductions of 3S1 and 4S2 witness the broader failure. The elliptic-conductor conclusion is restricted to the last two alternatives, with the actual rational cusp dP6 to W witnessing the broader failure. The signed-minor map, additive Chern-character identity, exact analytic/projective and elliptic/class-VII transports, finite Hopf covering, ruling/conductor maps, bounds and zero-Euler conclusions are proved. All literal receiving uses retain their required conclusions. The preproof computation and postrelease supplement are separately timed, and the latter adds no independent credit.",
